course: dictionary
lesson: 5442
title: One short word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some short words have more than one meaning. The clues around the word tell you which meaning is meant. «Lan» is one of these words, so look at the words near it before you decide.
explain: In computing, LAN stands for local area network: computers joined together in one building, like a school, so they can share printers and files. A «LAN party» is when friends link their computers to play games together.
explain: «Lan» is also a name or part of a name, and a fragment of longer words like «land» or «plan». A fragment is just a piece of a longer word, so in «land» the lan is not a word on its own.
explain: In Mandarin, «lán» means blue (蓝) and sounds like «lahn». «Lán sè» is the colour blue. In the made-up number code Kel, «ki lan pa» is 11: 2 times 5 is 10, and adding 1 makes 11.
fact: LAN stands for local area network, a set of computers joined together in one building.
fact: «Lan» can be a name, and a fragment of longer words like «land» and «plan».
fact: «Lán» is Mandarin for blue, and it sounds like «lahn». It is not an English word.
fact: In Kel, lan = 5, so «ki lan» means 2 times 5, which is 10.
fact: Clues such as computers, colours or numbers show which meaning of a word is being used.
exercise: In Kel, pa = 1, ki = 2, ro = 3, mu = 4 and lan = 5. What is «ki lan»? | *10 | 12 | 7 | 25
exercise: What does LAN stand for in computing? | *Local area network | Large Apple Network | Little adding node | Long alphabet number
exercise: In a Mandarin lesson, what does «lán sè» mean? | A type of train | *The colour blue | A small green garden | A school bell
test: In «land» and «plan», what is the part «lan»? | A computer network | *A small piece of a longer word | A name for a city | Mandarin for blue
test: In Kel, what is «ki lan pa»? | 16 | 9 | *11 | 10
exam: Why does the context matter when you see the word lan? | *Clues like computers, colours or numbers show which meaning is used | It only appears in the made-up code Kel | Lan is always a name | It always means the same thing, so no clues are needed
